{
  "name": "mite",
  "_about": "The red velvet mite (Trombidium holosericeum), 4 mm long: a plump scarlet body thick with velvety hair, narrowed in front where the small dark eyes sit on stalks; eight short red legs, the front pair the longest, held forward like feelers; small palps. It hunts tiny insects in leaf litter after rain. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
